    {
      "marker": "[c]",
      "text": "Students are strongly advised to take any one course from CHEM1280 or 1380 if they have not attained Level 3 or above in HKDSE Chemistry, or other equivalent qualifications.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[d]",
      "text": "Students are strongly advised to take either LSCI1001 or 1002 if they have not attained Level 3 or above in HKDSE Biology, or other equivalent qualifications. LSCI1001 is only for students who have not taken science courses with Biology component in HKDSE.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[e]",
      "text": "Students who fail ENGG1125 in Term 1 will have to retake the course in Term 2. The pre-assigned ENGG1130 in Term 2, will therefore be dropped.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[f]",
      "text": "Students who have declared to specialize in the ELITE Stream will be required to complete 6 units of ESTR4998 and 4999 to substitute for BMEG4998 and 4999.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[g]",
      "text": "Students are allowed to take a maximum of 3 units of CSCI course(s) at 1000 or above level.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[h]",
      "text": "Details of the entrance and coursework requirements, and declaration procedures for the ELITE Stream can be found at the ELITE website (www.erg.cuhk.edu.hk/erg/elite). Non-ELITE Engineering students may be allowed to take ESTR courses. Students are required to seek approval from their respective Major Programmes for using ESTR courses taken to fulfill the Major Programme Requirement. Details are available at the ELITE website.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[i]",
      "text": "Students can use up to 9 units of courses taken to fulfill the requirements of items 1 to 4 above to fulfill the elective requirements of the ELITE Stream. Item 3(b) Research Component Courses will not be included in these 9 units. A full list of ESTR courses is available at the ELITE website.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[j]",
      "text": "Students can use AIST/BMEG/CENG/CSCI/EEEN/ELEG/ENGG/IERG/MAEG/ SEEM research postgraduate courses at 5000 level to substitute for ESTR courses at 3000 or 4000 level, subject to the approval of the Stream Director and the Associate Dean (Education).",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[k]",
      "text": "The requirement of at least 3 units of Engineering courses at 5000 level is a requirement for the ELITE Stream only. It should not be interpreted as a requirement of the Major Programme.",
